B227/B227-p29-kingsmeadow-1500-1997.jpg","c":"Above: Fortythree years later and the old codger's still on the move! 24th August 1997 and Chas. (174) lines up for the Veterans A.C. 1500 metres Championship at Kingsmeadow. His time was ... well we won't go into that ... but is this a good case for euthanasia? Maybe we should pay him not to wear our club kit! Seriously though, 1,500 metres is now way over his best distance because in 1998 Chas became the Surrey County M70 Champion over 100 metres!\n\nThird from the left, standing back, is Dave McMullen and wearing 62 is 5,000 metre ace from the '50s and current UK Athletics Council Member - Chris Chataway.","id":"B227-62","w":"March 1999"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B227/B227-p29-kingsmeadow-1500-1997.jpg","caption":"Above: Fortythree years later and the old codger's still on the move! 24th August 1997 and Chas. (174) lines up for the Veterans A.C. 1500 metres Championship at Kingsmeadow. His time was ... well we won't go into that ... but is this a good case for euthanasia? Maybe we should pay him not to wear our club kit! Seriously though, 1,500 metres is now way over his best distance because in 1998 Chas became the Surrey County M70 Champion over 100 metres!\n\nThird from the left, standing back, is Dave McMullen and wearing 62 is 5,000 metre ace from the '50s and current UK Athletics Council Member - Chris Chataway.","source":"B227-62","when":"March 1999"},"slarchive":"https://slarchive.org/#athlete/dave-mcmullen","slRaces":1,"x":1,"share":{"d":"Dave McMullen in The Belgravian, the Belgrave Harriers club gazette, 1946–2001: 218 mentions in 59 issues, 165 race results and 1 photograph. Wrote or reported 2 items.","img":"https://belgravian-images.stephendgardner.workers.dev/belgravian/crops/B227/B227-p29-kingsmeadow-1500-1997.jpg","u":"https://stephengardner1.github.io/belgrave-harriers-data/belgravian/read/share/p-dave-mcmullen.html"},"legend":false}